439 - How Far From Home?
 / 
Key: Db
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 439
Topic: Early Advent - 

Verse 1:
[Db/F]How far from home? I [Ab7/Gb]asked, as [Bbm]on I bent my [Db]steps—the watchman [Ab7]spake:
[Gb]"The long, dark [Db]night is almost gone, The [Ab7/Gb]morning [Bbm]soon will break.
[Db]Then weep no more, [Ab7/Eb]but speed thy [Fm]flight, With Hope's [Db]bright star thy [Ab7/Eb]guiding ray,
[Gb]Till thou shalt [Db]reach the realms of [Ab7/Eb]light, In everlasting [Db/Ab]day."

Verse 2:
[Db/F]I asked the [Ab7/Gb]warrior [Bbm]on [Db]the [Ab7/Eb]field;
[Db/F]This was his [Ab7/Gb]soul-inspiring song:
[Gb]"With courage, [Db/F]bold, the [Ab7/Gb]sword I'll [Bbm]wield,
[Gb]The [Db]battle is [Ab7/Gb]not [Bbm]long.
[Db]Then weep [Ab7/Eb]no more, [Fm]but [Db]well endure
[Db]The conflict, [Ab7]till [Fm]thy [Db]work is [Ab7/Eb]done;
[Gb]For this [Db/Ab]we know, [Ab7/Eb]the prize [Gb]is [Db]sure,
[Gb]When [Db]victory [Gb]is [Db]won."

Verse 3:
[Db/F]I asked again; [Bbm]earth, sea, [Db]and [Ab7/Eb]sun
[Db/F]Seemed, with one [Ab7/Gb]voice, [Bbm]to make [Db]reply:
[Gb]"Time's [Db]wasting sands are [Ab7/Gb]nearly [Bbm]run,
[Gb]Eternity [Ab7/Gb]is [Bbm]nigh.
[Db]Then weep [Ab7/Eb]no more-with [Db]warning [Ab7/Eb]tones,
[Db]Portentous [Ab7]signs [Fm]are thickening [Ab7/Eb]round,
[Gb]The whole [Db]creation, [Ab7]waiting, [Db]groans,
[Gb]To [Db]hear the [Ab7/Eb]trumpet [Db]sound."

Verse 4:
[Db/F]Not far from [Ab7/Gb]home! [Bbm]O [Db]blessed [Ab7/Eb]thought!
[Db/F]The traveler's [Ab7/Gb]lonely [Db]heart to [Ab7/Eb]cheer;
[Gb]Which oft [Db/Ab]a healing [Ab7/Gb]balm has [Bbm]brought,
[Gb]And [Db]dried the mourner's [Bbm]tear.
[Db]Then weep [Ab7/Eb]no more, [Fm]since [Db]we shall [Ab7/Eb]meet
[Db]Where weary [Ab7]footsteps [Db]never [Ab7/Eb]roam-
[Gb]Our trails [Db/Ab]past, our [Ab7/Eb]joys [Gb]complete,
[Gb]Safe [Db]in our [Ab7/Eb]Father's [Db]home.
